  "nl_text": "The database schema named 'schemabench_0088' contains 9 tables. The primary purpose of this schema is to manage user experience and achievement tracking.\nThe 'users' table represents the users of the application. It has a primary key 'id' and a foreign key 'level_id' referencing the 'levels' table. The 'levels' table represents the different levels a user can achieve in the application.\nThe 'streaks' table is used to track user activity streaks. It has a primary key 'id', foreign keys 'user_id' and 'activity_id' referencing the 'users' and 'streak_activities' tables respectively, and several other columns including 'count', 'activity_at', 'frozen_until', 'created_at', and 'updated_at'.\nThe 'streak_histories' table is used to track the history of user activity streaks. It has a primary key 'id', foreign keys 'user_id' and 'streak_activity_id' referencing the 'users' and 'streak_activities' tables respectively, and several other columns including 'count', 'started_at', 'ended_at', 'created_at', and 'updated_at'.\nThe 'streak_activities' table represents the different activities that can be tracked in the application. It has a primary key 'id', and several other columns including 'name', 'description', 'created_at', and 'updated_at'.\nThe 'experiences' table is used to track user experience points and levels. It has a primary key 'id', foreign keys 'user_id' and 'level_id' referencing the 'users' and 'levels' tables respectively, and a column 'experience_points' with a default value of 0.\nThe 'experience_audits' table is used to track changes in user experience points and levels. It has a primary key 'id', a foreign key 'user_id' referencing the 'users' table, and several other columns including 'points', 'levelled_up', 'level_to', 'type', 'reason', 'created_at', and 'updated_at'.\nThe 'achievements' table represents the achievements that can be earned by users. It has a primary key 'id', and several other columns including 'name', 'is_secret', 'description', 'image', 'created_at', and 'updated_at'.\nThe 'achievement_user' table is used to track which users have earned which achievements. It has a primary key 'id', foreign keys 'user_id' and 'achievement_id' referencing the 'users' and 'achievements' tables respectively, and a column 'progress'. The 'users' table has foreign key references to this table, indicating that each user can have multiple achievements. The 'achievements' table has foreign key references to this table, indicating that each achievement can be earned by multiple users.",
  "gold_question": "1) Background / Context\n\nLevel Up is a Laravel package designed to integrate gamification elements into web applications. Gamification is used to enhance user interaction by adding game-like mechanics in non-gaming contexts, thereby increasing user engagement and retention.\n\n2) Objectives\n\nThe main objective of Level Up is to provide a flexible tool that incorporates gamification elements such as user levels, experience points, streaks, achievements, and leaderboards into Laravel applications. It aims to promote user engagement, cultivate a competitive environment, and make user interactions more enjoyable.\n\n3) Stakeholders & Users\n\n- Application Developers: Implement the Level Up package in their Laravel projects to enhance user interaction.\n- End Users: Interact with the gamification elements to earn rewards and track progress, thus enhancing their engagement.\n- Business Stakeholders: Gain benefits from increased user retention and activity.\n\n4) Functional Descriptions\n\n- User Levels: Users are assigned levels based on experience points earned from interactions.\n- Experience Points (XP): Users accumulate XP through various activities within the application.\n- Streaks: Track user activity streaks, incentivizing regular interaction and engagement.\n- Achievements: Users unlock achievements as they meet predefined criteria, which may or may not be visible to them.\n- Leaderboards: Display user rankings based on XP to foster competition.\n- Customization: Allow developers to configure and customize gamification features to suit specific application needs.\n\n5) Non-Functional Descriptions\n\n- Scalability: Should support efficient performance even as user numbers grow.\n- Security: Ensure user data and activities are processed and stored securely.\n- Usability: The system should be intuitive for both developers integrating it and users engaging with the gamification features.\n- Maintainability: Code and database structures should facilitate easy maintenance and updates.",
  "input_json": "/data/SchemaBench/Experiment/schema2text_deepseek/0088.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: schemabench_0088\nCREATE TABLE `users` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `level_id` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `users_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`level_id`) REFERENCES `levels` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `levels` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `streaks` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `activity_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `count` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `activity_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `frozen_until` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `created_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `updated_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `streaks_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `users` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `streaks_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`activity_id`) REFERENCES `streak_activities` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `streak_histories` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `streak_activity_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `count` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `started_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `ended_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `created_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `updated_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `streak_histories_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `users` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `streak_histories_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`streak_activity_id`) REFERENCES `streak_activities` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `streak_activities` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `description` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `created_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `updated_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `experiences` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `level_id` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `experience_points` int(11) DEFAULT 0,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `experiences_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `users` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `experiences_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`level_id`) REFERENCES `levels` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `experience_audits` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `points` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `levelled_up` tinyint(1) NOT NULL,\n  `level_to` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `type` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `reason` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `created_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `updated_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `experience_audits_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `users` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `achievements` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `is_secret` tinyint(1) NOT NULL,\n  `description` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `image` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `created_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `updated_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `achievement_user` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `achievement_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `progress` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `achievement_user_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `users` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `achievement_user_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`achievement_id`) REFERENCES `achievements` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
